/-!
# The geometric input of [Stacks, Tag 0GA1], assembled on the blowup

`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityII`
`.exists_pow_le_annihilator_tor_quotient_pow_of_abutsTo_restrictScalars` is [Stacks, Tag 0GA1]
granted a hypothesis `hSS`: for every `A`-module `M`, every `i ≥ t` and every `q ≥ q₀`, a
cohomological spectral sequence of `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`-modules which abuts to a graded
family whose degree `-i` term is `Tor_i^A(M, Iᑫ)` after restriction of scalars, whose terms along
the antidiagonal of degree `-i` are annihilated by the image of `Iᶜ`, and which vanishes outside
a band of `N` columns. This file produces that spectral sequence at the hypercohomology spectral
sequence [Stacks, Tag 0G9Q] of `Lp^*M̃(q)` on the blowup `p : X ⟶ Spec A` of `Spec A` in `I`, so
nothing is assumed any longer.

The four clauses are instantiated as follows, with
`K := Stacks.Blowup.twistedDerivedPullbackQcoh I M q` and
`S := Stacks.Cohomology.FilteredComplex.hypercohomologySpectralSequence X.toRingedSpace K.obj`.

* **Abutment.** `AlgebraicGeometry.hypercohomologySpectralSequence_abutsTo` at `X` and `K`; the
  blowup is quasi-compact and quasi-separated for `A` Noetherian, and `K` is the twisted derived
  pullback with its quasi-coherent cohomology.
* **Band.** `AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_hypercohomologySpectralSequence_page_two` at the same data,
  with `N` the uniform vanishing bound
  `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isZero_rightDerivedPlus_groupSections` of `X`, read at the row
  `-i - p`: the column index alone decides.
* **Annihilation.** `Stacks.Cohomology.FilteredComplex`
  `.mem_annihilator_hypercohomologySpectralSequence_page_two` with the central endomorphism
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.terminalSectionToEnd` of the global function attached to `r ∈ Iᶜ`,
  whose vanishing on `H^j(K)` is
  `Stacks.Blowup.exists_pow_le_center_app_homology_twistedDerivedPullback_eq_zero`
  ([Stacks, Tag 0GA0]) at a K-flat resolution chosen by
  `CochainComplex.KFlat.exists_kFlat_resolution`. That statement needs `j ≤ -t`, so it covers
  the rows `-i - p` with `p ≥ 0`, which is every row the band keeps: for `p < 0` the term is
  already zero and every scalar annihilates it. The ideal generated by the image of `Iᶜ` is then
  below the annihilator because the annihilator is an ideal.
* **Abutment identification.** `AlgebraicGeometry.baseHypercohomologyIso` reads the abutment of
  `S` over `A` as the cohomology of `A`-linear derived global sections, which
  [Stacks, Tag 0G9Z] — `Stacks.Blowup`
  `.exists_threshold_nonempty_derivedGlobalSectionsTwistedPullback_iso_derivedTensorIdealPow`,
  unconditional — identifies with `M ⊗^𝐋_A Iᑫ`, whose degree `-i` cohomology is `Tor_i^A(M, Iᑫ)`
  by `AdicCompletionTor.nonempty_derivedTensorSingleHomology_iso_Tor'`. The restriction of
  scalars `AlgebraicGeometry.restrictScalarsOver (Stacks.Blowup.toSpec I)` is
  `ModuleCat.restrictScalars (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpCoeffScalar I)` by `rfl`, so the ring
  homomorphism the bridge is fed is `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpCoeffScalar I`.

With `hSS` discharged, [Stacks, Tag 0GA1] holds with no hypothesis beyond the Situation of
[Stacks, Tag 0G9W] — `A` Noetherian and `I` generated by at most `t` elements. The transition
statements [Stacks, Tag 0GA2] and [Stacks, Tag 0GA3] are deduced from it in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityII.UniformTorTransition` and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityII.UniformVanishingConditions`,
which import this file.

[Stacks, Tag 0GA4] is *not* reached from here. Its hypothesis is the uniform annihilation above
`d = dim A` for a Noetherian local ring, whereas [Stacks, Tag 0GA1] gives it above the number of
generators of `I`, and an ideal of a local ring need not be generated by `dim A` elements.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_hypercohomologySpectralSequence_abutsTo_tor_idealPow`: the spectral
  sequence on the blowup that the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0GA1] runs on.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityII.exists_pow_le_annihilator_tor_quotient_pow_blowup`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0GA1].**

